  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that multiprofile RNA with PCA and avgpool is clearly best (config_002: acc 0.591, F1 0.573), while single-profile RNA and transformer aggregation are weaker, and image-only ResNet is poor. The key remaining uncertainty is whether a stronger RNA representation can improve the already promising multiprofile avgpool setting. config_008 changes only the RNA encoder from PCA to scGPT while keeping profile setting and aggregation fixed, so it cleanly tests representation quality. This is a focused exploitation of the current best direction and more informative than moving to image or multimodal settings with weak image evidence."
